  "patch_scope": "Bazel-compatible core set methods/constructor, assignment-specific mutation, scoped iterator error cleanup and regressions; allocation-free typed BigInt inspection for native JSON preflight; Bazel 9.3 UTF-8 byte-string string methods (ASCII-only case mapping/predicates, ASCII strip whitespace, explicit None strip argument, byte-wise title letter state) and Printer-compatible string repr escaping; location-aware indexing and `in` (StarlarkValue::at_with_location / is_in_with_location with default delegation to at / is_in, used by the ArrayIndex and In bytecode instructions with the expression's lazily computed span) for native ctx.toolchains string keys (docs/TOOLCHAINS.md). Native feature installation remains separate from vendor changes. Bazel 9.3 frozen list/dict mutation text ('trying to mutate a frozen list|dict value', Starlark.checkMutable) and a reverse `|` hook (StarlarkValue::rbit_or) so a dict left operand defers to `select()` (SelectorList.binaryOp with thisLeft = false), also for `|=`.",
